{"authored" [{"question" "q-19107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,1,-1)$, $B(3,-2,2)$, and $C(-1,-2,1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,1,-1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-2,2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,2⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,2⟩\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}})≈{54}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c4ae64d9a3b82d1d472628be6b7d38a56c75262d035fbf1513196b1932ceac9" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{112}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{18}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{48}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{54}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{88}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{54}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $a\\cdot b=-9$, find the angle between $a=⟨-2t,3t⟩$ and $b=⟨3,1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $a\\cdot b=-9$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-9 \\\\ -2t\\cdot 3+3t\\cdot 1 & =-9 \\\\ -6t+3t & =-9 \\\\ -3t & =-9 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨-2(3),\\,3(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{9}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{117}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{3\\sqrt{13}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{130}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{130}})≈{105.3}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathaca