e/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $c\\cdot d=11$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & =11 \\\\ 2t\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3 & =11 \\\\ 4t+3 & =11 \\\\ 4t & =8 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =⟨2(2),1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $c$ and $d$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{|\\,c\\,||\\,d\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{17}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{221}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{221}})≈{42.27}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69439c99388ed4f03cb7c64633545f69bd84ad1aacf06d4f3cc7b3d16b3e60a7" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category"