me/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{52.33}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $p\\cdot q=11$, find the angle between $p=⟨t,t-1⟩$ and $q=⟨-4,-1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $p\\cdot q=11$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =11 \\\\ t\\cdot (-4)+(t-1)\\cdot (-1) & =11 \\\\ -4t-t+1 & =11 \\\\ -5t & =10 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨(-2),(-2)-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $p$ and $q$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,p\\,||\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{13}\\cdot \\sqrt{17}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{221}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{221}})≈{42.3}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "69439c99388ed4f03cb7c64633545f69bd84ad1aacf06d4f3cc7b3d16b3e60a7" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{39.9}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db24