783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{42.3}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/state.json" "file_sha256" "4dd2b2e8ac76d909cd281dd7f76db2480c774e0d1ef1ca5de3a6c5b783492a5c" "basis" 1679 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-19032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $c\\cdot d=11$, find the angle between $c=⟨2t,1⟩$ and $d=⟨2,3⟩.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-19032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $c\\cdot d=11$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & =11 \\\\ 2t\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3 & =11 \\\\ 4t+3 & =11 \\\\ 4t & =8 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =⟨2(2),1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $c$ and $d$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{|\\,c\\,||\\,d\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{17}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{221}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{221}})≈{42.27}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-19032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d7c89df0cfbc2ba35bf43dc47e6f5a4789b33e356c10d1ef92101b9c4158735d"} {"question" "q-19032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-19032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{33.74}^{∘}"] ["math" "{37.75}^{∘}"] ["math" "{42.27}^{∘}"] ["math" "{46.18}^{∘}"] ["math" "{52.33}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-19032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{42.27}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,1,-1)$, $B(3,-2,2)$, and $C(-1,-2,1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,1,-1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-2,2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,2⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,2⟩\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}})≈{54}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d7c89df0cfbc2ba35bf43dc47e6f5a4789b33e356c10d1ef92101b9c4158735d"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{112}^{∘}"] ["math" "{18}^{∘}"] ["math" "{48}^{∘}"] ["math" "{54}^{∘}"] ["math" "{88}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{54}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-101506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(1,5,-1)$, $Q(5,1,1)$, and $R(2,5,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-101506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨1,5,-1⟩,\\,q=⟨5,1,1⟩,\\,r=⟨2,5,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩-⟨1,5,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-4,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨2,5,0⟩-⟨1,5,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{36}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={45}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-101506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d7c89df0cfbc2ba35bf43dc47e6f5a4789b33e356c10d1ef92101b9c4158735d"} {"question" "q-101506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-101506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0}^{∘}"] ["math" "{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "{45}^{∘}"] ["math" "{60}^{∘}"] ["math" "{90}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-101506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{45}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-101515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $p\\cdot q=11$, find the angle between $p=⟨t,t-1⟩$ and $q=⟨-4,-1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-101515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $p\\cdot q=11$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =11 \\\\ t\\cdot (-4)+(t-1)\\cdot (-1) & =11 \\\\ -4t-t+1 & =11 \\\\ -5t & =10 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨(-2),(-2)-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $p$ and $q$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,p\\,||\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{13}\\cdot \\sqrt{17}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{221}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{221}})≈{42.3}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-101515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d7c89df0cfbc2ba35bf43dc47e6f5a4789b33e356c10d1ef92101b9c4158735d"} {"question" "q-101515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-101515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{39.9}^{∘}"] ["math" "{40.5}^{∘}"] ["math" "{42.3}^{∘}"] ["math" "{44.4}^{∘}"] ["math" "{45.1}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-101515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{42.3}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-125078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $a\\cdot b=-9$, find the angle between $a=⟨-2t,3t⟩$ and $b=⟨3,1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-125078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $a\\cdot b=-9$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-9 \\\\ -2t\\cdot 3+3t\\cdot 1 & =-9 \\\\ -6t+3t & =-9 \\\\ -3t & =-9 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨-2(3),\\,3(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{9}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{117}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{3\\sqrt{13}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{130}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{130}})≈{105.3}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-125078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d7c89df0cfbc2ba35bf43dc47e6f5a4789b33e356c10d1ef92101b9c4158735d"} {"question" "q-125078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-125078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{100.5}^{∘}"] ["math" "{105.3}^{∘}"] ["math" "{115.2}^{∘}"] ["math" "{123.2}^{∘}"] ["math" "{95.9}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"} {"question" "q-125078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{105.3}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/state.json" "file_sha256" "af8cecf034a01ec2428da3842a9aea0c439f21a1659c356b8941948dfddc4686"}] "usage" {"q-125078" [] "q-19032" [] "q-19107" [] "q-101515" []} "basis" 1697 "retractions" [[17592186269129 :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,1,-1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-2,2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,2⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,2⟩\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}})≈{54}^{∘}.\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186269131 17592186269132 17592186269133 17592186269134 17592186269135 17592186299813 17592186299814 17592186299815 17592186299816 17592186299817 17592186325340 17592186325341 17592186325342 17592186325343 17592186325344 17592186325354 17592186325355 17592186325356 17592186325357 17592186325358] "immutable_fields" [[17592186269130 :answer-field/correct] [17592186269130 :answer-field/id] [17592186269130 :answer-field/key] [17592186269130 :answer-field/type] [17592186299812 :answer-field/correct] [17592186299812 :answer-field/id] [17592186299812 :answer-field/key] [17592186299812 :answer-field/type] [17592186325339 :answer-field/correct] [17592186325339 :answer-field/id] [17592186325339 :answer-field/key] [17592186325339 :answer-field/type] [17592186325353 :answer-field/correct] [17592186325353 :answer-field/id] [17592186325353 :answer-field/key] [17592186325353 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
